---
import './operations.css';
const stages=['Client wait','Transit and reply','Command execution','Decode and return'];
---
<figure class="ops-figure" data-ops-latency>
 <figcaption><span>Figure 2</span> The same thirty milliseconds, spent elsewhere</figcaption>
 <div class="ops-scene">
  <div class="trace-summary"><b data-live data-total>Cache lookup: 30 ms</b><small>One successful GET · invented trace</small></div>
  <div class="timeline" aria-hidden="true">{stages.map((_,i)=><div data-segment={i}><span>{i+1}</span></div>)}<i data-cursor></i></div>
  <div class="scale"><span>0 ms</span><span>15 ms</span><span>30 ms</span></div>
  <div class="trace-legend" data-live>{stages.map((label,i)=><div data-stage={i}><b>{i+1}. {label}</b><span data-duration={i}></span></div>)}</div>
  <p class="ops-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Choose a trace, then follow its wait.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="ops-controls"><label>Where the time goes <select data-case><option value="command">Command is slow</option><option value="client">Client is waiting</option></select></label><div class="ops-buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span></div><div class="ops-hold" data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <p class="ops-caption">The bands add up to one cache lookup. Transit combines the outward and return trips for this accounting view. It does not mean the reply travels before execution. A miss would add source admission, a source read and possibly a fill after this lookup.</p>
 <details><summary>Traces as text</summary><p>Slow command: 2 ms client wait, 4 ms communication, 22 ms command execution, 2 ms decoding. Waiting client: 24 ms client wait, 3 ms communication, 1 ms execution, 2 ms decoding. Both total 30 ms. Only command execution falls inside the slow log’s timer.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-ops-latency]').forEach(root=>{
 const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case]')!;
 const cursor=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cursor]')!;
 let previous=''; let animation:Animation|undefined;
 const draw=(step:number)=>{
  const client=select.value==='client', times=client?[24,3,1,2]:[2,4,22,2];
  root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-segment]').forEach((el,i)=>{el.style.width=`${times[i]/30*100}%`;el.classList.toggle('passed',i<step)});
  root.querySelectorAll('[data-duration]').forEach((el,i)=>el.textContent=`${times[i]} ms`);
  root.querySelectorAll('[data-stage]').forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('active',i===step-1));
  const end=times.slice(0,step).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/30*100;
  const start=times.slice(0,Math.max(0,step-1)).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/30*100;
  cursor.style.left=`${end}%`;
  const key=`${select.value}:${step}`;
  if(previous!==key){animation?.cancel();if(step&&!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)animation=cursor.animate([{left:`${start}%`},{left:`${end}%`}],{duration:700,easing:'ease-in-out'});previous=key;}
  const descriptions=[
   'The application waits thirty milliseconds for a usable cached card. The total alone cannot locate the delay.',
   client?'Twenty-four milliseconds pass before the command can proceed. Inspect client scheduling and, for clients that queue, pool acquisition. Redis has not executed the GET yet.':'The client spends two milliseconds preparing the operation. Most of this trace’s delay lies ahead.',
   `Communication accounts for ${times[1]} milliseconds. Connection setup, network delay and reply transfer belong to the client-visible path, outside the command execution timer.`,
   client?'Redis executes GET in one millisecond. A quiet slow log is consistent with this thirty-millisecond lookup; investigate the client wait.':'Command execution takes twenty-two milliseconds. Correlate the request with server execution evidence before changing the cache deployment.',
   'Decoding and validation take the final two milliseconds. The application can now return a valid hit. Keep the whole lookup inside the request deadline.'
  ];root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=descriptions[step];
 };
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw});select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
});
</script>
<style>
.trace-summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1rem}.timeline{display:flex;position:relative;height:62px;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface)}.timeline>div{box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-right:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);color:var(--color-text-secondary);transition:width .5s ease}.timeline>div.passed{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 18%,var(--color-surface));color:var(--color-text)}.timeline i{position:absolute;top:-7px;bottom:-7px;width:3px;background:var(--teal);transform:translateX(-2px)}.timeline span{font: .8rem var(--font-mono)}.scale{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:.75rem var(--font-mono);margin:.7rem 0 1rem}.trace-legend{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.trace-legend>div{padding:.6rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface)}.trace-legend b,.trace-legend span{display:block}.trace-legend b{font-size:.8rem}.trace-legend .active{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:-2px}.trace-legend span{font-family:var(--font-mono)}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.timeline>div{transition:none}}
</style>
